his is a list of skills in The Sims 4. Skills can be earned by interacting with the various gameplay items associated with them.

The game features a variety of skill types. For Teens and older, these include Major Skills (Level 10 Skills) as well as Minor Skills (Level 5 Skills). There are some exceptions to this however, such as the Vampire Lore Skill, which has 15 Levels.

For Children and Toddlers, their core skills are referred to as Fundamentals and include some variation in the maximum level one can achieve, such as the Potty Skill, which only has 3 Levels. Toddler skills also correspond to child skills. This means that if a toddler ages up with certain skill levels, it will result in improvements in the child skills they correspond to:

Toddler Skill	Child Skill
Trait TS4 Gregarious	Communication	Skill TS4 Social	Social
Skill TS4 Imagination	Imagination	Skill TS4 Creative	Creativity
Skill TS4 Movement	Movement	Skill TS4 Motor	Motor
Trait TS4 Child's Play	Thinking	Skill TS4 Mental	Mental
Skill TS4 Potty	Potty	N/A

If a toddler ages up with a movement skill level 4, they will start their child life stage at motor skill level 2 and 44% of the current motor skill bar completed (consequently, they have 56% to go to get to motor skill level 3). If a toddler has reached at least level 3 in four skills, then they will get a Happy Toddler bonus trait, which boosts all skill gains by 10%. If a toddler has reached the maximum level in all fundamentals (except Potty), then they will get a Top Notch Toddler bonus trait, which boosts all skill and career gains by 25%:

Toddler Skill Level	Child Skill Level Completed (and % left to next level)
1
None
2
1 and 45% of next level (55% to level 2)
3
1 and 90% of next level (10% to level 2)
4
2 and 44% of next level (56% to level 3)
5
2 and 94% of next level (6% to level 3)

